results.content:
I've been using this app since 2018, and I have only compliments for it. Recently I updated my Mac and that consequently updated Xmind, so I was met with both positive and negative changes. I really appreciate that more features are made available to the free version, especially adding images. I wasn't so pleased with the downsize in the marker options. Personally, I liked the wide range of options that I could use to tag topics in my mind maps, but now, there are only a few that are even usable. Seriously, what is the point of downsizing it? I also think that the color menu should use the system utility, because it is MUCH easier to save colors there, while the Xmind color menu does not let you save colors and has ugly colors indeed. [...] 1. Added a collaborative version of the Outliner for real-time editing;
2. Added a favorites/starred entry so you can quickly access bookmarked maps;
3. Create with AI can now turn images into mind maps via image attachments;
4. Added Data Masking, accessible through a right-click flow in the editor for international version;
5. Fixed an issue where Map Shot screenshots captured inaccurate content;
6. Fixed an issue where the sheet Bar displayed abnormally in ZEN mode;
7. Improved the interaction experience of the scrollbar within the editor;
8. Fixed various other known issues.

Fixed other known issues. [...] 1. Fresh New Look: A lighter, more focused experience across the Home and map editor.
2. Enhanced Zones: Auto-resize, connect to other topics with relationships, and more.
3. Xmind AI now supports web search when generating mind maps.
4. Xmind AI now supports Grow Ideas from a selected topic with one click.
5. Improved the collaboration experience for online files.
6. Supported displaying all notes in the mind map with one click.
7. Added a keyboard shortcut for text underline.
8. Task now supports displaying dates in British format.
9. Fixed an issue where images exported from topics containing emoji displayed incorrect styles.
10. Fixed an issue where certain features in Custom Themes behaved unexpectedly.
